{"condition": "sttp", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "index": 279, "expected": "6", "prediction": "6", "correct": true, "result": {"text": "Let $R$ be Ruby's current age and $S$ be Sam's current age.\n\nFrom the first statement, \"Ruby is 6 times older than Sam,\" we can write the equation:\n$$R = 6S$$\n\nFrom the second statement, \"In 9 years, Ruby will be 3 times as old as Sam,\" we can write the equation for their ages in 9 years:\n$$R + 9 = 3(S + 9)$$\n\nNow, substitute the value of $R$ from the first equation into the second equation:\n$$6S + 9 = 3(S + 9)$$\n\nExpand the right side of the equation:\n$$6S + 9 = 3S + 27$$\n\nSubtract $3S$ from both sides to group the $S$ terms:\n$$3S + 9 = 27$$\n\nSubtract 9 from both sides to isolate the term with $S$:\n$$3S = 18$$\n\nDivide by 3 to solve for $S$:\n$$S = 6$$\n\nSo, Sam is currently 6 years old.\n(Check: If Sam is 6, Ruby is $6 \\times 6 = 36$. In 9 years, Sam will be 15 and Ruby will be 45. $45$ is indeed $3$ times $15$.)\n\n#### 6\n", "token_ids": [9764, 393, 49, 3, 381, 22984, 579, 1428, 4092, 321, 393, 50, 3, 381, 7967, 579, 1428, 4092, 13, 271, 3702, 279, 1118, 4952, 11, 328, 59633, 369, 220, 21, 2942, 8742, 1056, 7967, 1288, 567, 628, 3165, 279, 22868, 25, 198, 13682, 49, 283, 220, 21, 50, 13682, 271, 3702, 279, 2018, 4952, 11, 328, 623, 220, 24, 1578, 11, 22984, 668, 381, 220, 18, 2942, 430, 2235, 430, 7967, 1288, 567, 628, 3165, 279, 22868, 364, 836, 16149, 303, 220, 24, 1578, 25, 198, 13682, 49, 478, 220, 24, 283, 220, 18, 3631, 478, 220, 24, 8, 13682, 271, 6820, 11, 26782, 279, 869, 314, 393, 49, 3, 494, 279, 1118, 22868, 1083, 279, 2018, 22868, 25, 198, 13682, 21, 50, 478, 220, 24, 283, 220, 18, 3631, 478, 220, 24, 8, 13682, 271, 37657, 279, 1245, 3008, 314, 279, 22868, 25, 198, 13682, 21, 50, 478, 220, 24, 283, 220, 18, 50, 478, 220, 17, 22, 13682, 271, 3036, 2076, 393, 18, 50, 3, 494, 2107, 10744, 310, 1809, 279, 393, 50, 3, 3665, 25, 198, 13682, 18, 50, 478, 220, 24, 283, 220, 17, 22, 13682, 271, 3036, 2076